      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "a_init_alloc_must_reserve_token_probe",
      "fine_trace_step": 5,
      "description": "Root cause. When callers build a parse target with `size == 0`, vulnerable `coap_pdu_init()` allocates only `max_hdr_size` bytes and places `pdu->token` exactly at the end of that allocation. The fix changes this allocation to reserve at least two payload bytes so the later extended-token probes in `coap_pdu_parse_header()` cannot read past the buffer."
    },
